{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179570-the-art-of-the-deal","id":1179570,"title":"The Art of the Deal","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-26T12:25:11-08:00","id":1179570,"title":"The Art of the Deal","content":"So: I want to make a mage who can do the sort of things that changelings and demons can do: forge a mystical pact with another person that gives both parties something they want so long as both meet their obligations. I don't know if <b>Mage</b> already covers this; if so, could someone please or where? <br /> <br /> It seems to me that Deal-making would involve Space (for its Sympathetic aspects, not its distances-and-measurements stuff) as the Deal creates a mystical connection between the involved parties; and Fate, for its ability to impose consequences for actions (both in the form of rewards for honoring the Deal and punishments for breaking it). But beyond that, I'm not sure how it would work.<br /> <br /> Suggestions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T12:38:36-08:00","id":1179576,"title":"","content":"Maybe summon a Supernal Fae, to serve as Notary and Backer of the deal? Space for the connections might be better for doing the &quot;they're my friends/spouse/dog now&quot; kinds of deals that Unchained make.<br /> <br /> This <i>actually</i> doesn't seem to be an area Mage covers well. Consequences? Sure. Deals where the deal itself offers power? No so much. Spells are backed by their source's (in this case, the Mage) power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-26-2018, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T12:45:07-08:00","id":1179577,"title":"","content":"I feel like this is covered pretty well by Oaths Fulfilled and Sworn Oaths. The consequences of breaking or keeping a deal can be built out in interesting ways via custom Conditions and Tilts. In what way isn\u2019t this all just part of Fate\u2019s purview?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T13:20:27-08:00","id":1179588,"title":"","content":"Hmm\u2026 fair enough, especially after noting that Interconnections (Fate \u2022) lets you detect Sympathetic connections, indicating that you don't always need Space when Sympathy is involved.<br /> <br /> EDIT: although\u2026 it occurs to me that using Sworn Oaths on multiple subjects at once might not result in a single, shared agreement: each participant would be bound by his own Oath independent of the other parties. Space could be used to tie the Oaths together so that the first to break their Oath is the only one to suffer the consequences: the others lose their boons, but they don't turn into hexes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-26-2018, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T13:37:39-08:00","id":1179594,"title":"","content":"Why would other subjects who are upholding their end of the bargain lose their Boon? The only scenario I can think of where that would happen is if part of their Oaths required them to keep any other parties from failing in their own Oaths, in which case they\u2019d also get Hexed.<br /> <br /> Basically, one person in a multiple subject Sworn Oath doesn\u2019t have the power to switch off the benefits for other subjects by breaking his own Oath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T13:46:22-08:00","id":1179596,"title":"","content":"I agree that that's how a strictly Fate-based multiple-subject Sworn Oath would work. I'm suggesting that <i>by adding Space to it</i>, you might be able to create a single, <i>shared</i> Oath, rather than a Web of related Oaths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T13:50:02-08:00","id":1179599,"title":"","content":"I think the easiest way to do that would simply be to use Shared Fate. All subjects uphold the same oath or suffer the consequences together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T14:57:22-08:00","id":1179629,"title":"","content":"You could rule that AoE <i>Swearing the Oath</i> is a single shared oath and individually targeting gets you distinct effects.<br /> <br /> That said, another approach would be to have the benefits and the responsibility apply to a group <i>as a specific target</i>. To truly join the group, one would need to swear the oath, but then they would be added to the group. If a person gets kicked out or forswears the group, they wouldn't affect the oath from thenceforth. That kind of thing could be generational. Space and Mind do have an arguable role in this but you could still rule it as Fate-only..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T16:22:21-08:00","id":1179652,"title":"","content":"And now I\u2019m imagining a Legacy built on \u201cthe devil at the crossroads\u201d concept, offering deals and bargains to those who seek it. Using Fate and Space magic, their Attainments sidestepping some of the laws of magic those Arcana typically follow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T16:31:56-08:00","id":1179655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179570-the-art-of-the-deal?p=1179629#post1179629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could rule that AoE <i>Swearing the Oath</i> is a single shared oath and individually targeting gets you distinct effects.<br /> <br /> That said, another approach would be to have the benefits and the responsibility apply to a group <i>as a specific target</i>. To truly join the group, one would need to swear the oath, but then they would be added to the group. If a person gets kicked out or forswears the group, they wouldn't affect the oath from thenceforth. That kind of thing could be generational. Space and Mind do have an arguable role in this but you could still rule it as Fate-only..</div> </div> </div> </div>An AoE Sworn Oath would only remain in place on subjects while they\u2019re inside the area prescribed by the Scale of the of the AoE. Once you walk out of it Sworn Oaths no longer applies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T16:38:21-08:00","id":1179658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1179570-the-art-of-the-deal?p=1179652#post1179652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now I\u2019m imagining a Legacy built on \u201cthe devil at the crossroads\u201d concept, offering deals and bargains to those who seek it. Using Fate and Space magic, their Attainments sidestepping some of the laws of magic those Arcana typically follow.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the nice things about legacies is that attainments don\u2019t take spell control slots. This means you could make as many magically enforced deals as you want all running simultaneously. I used that as a basis for when I attempted to update Keepers of the Covenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T23:11:22-08:00","id":1179760,"title":"","content":"Two words: Conditional Duration. Just make the subject breaking their promise be what ends the buff spell early.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}